<title>SWEDEN: Skanska says wins Czech Republic contract.</title>
<headline>Skanska says wins Czech Republic contract.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction company Skanska said on Thursday it had won a new construction order in the Czech Republic worth $9.5 million.</p>
<p>The order from Swedish forestry company AssiDoman involved building a plant at Zebrack, 40 kms southeast of Prague, for the production of packaging material.</p>
<p>The plant will be about 23,000 square metres.</p>
<p>Construction will start immediately and is expected to be completed within a year, Skanska said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1045</p>
